      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "2. The present petition has been preferred for the following reliefs:\n(i) for issuance of a writ in the nature of mandamus directing respondents authority the to concern the pay compensation for the land acquired by the authorities mentioned in paragraph no.6 of the present writ application as per the Patna High Bindeshwari Prasad Yadav vs The Union Of India on 16 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/119714369/\n1 Court CWJC No.2076 of 2024(2) dt.16-05-2024 present rate prevailing as per the Right Fair Compensation and Transparency in land, Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 read with The Right Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land, Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Rules, 2014 and further amendments rate of interest along with litigation cost to the petitioner;\n(ii) for quashing of (Annexure-6) order dated 29.08.2023 passed by respondent no.\n06, Arbitrator-cum- commissioner, Magadh Division, Gaya passed in Arbitration Case No. 115 of 2021 in the matter of Bindeshwari Prasad Yadav Versus the Competent Authority cum Land Acquisition Officer, Nawada and others;\n(iii) for quashing of (Annexure-5) the award No.29 dated 13.01.2020 in Land Acquisition Case No.\n1/19-20 in the name of the petitioner and others, for an amount of Rs. 8,39,813/- for an area of 0.0839 acres of land in the name of the petitioner and his brother award passed by competent authority cum District Land Acquisition officer, Nawada under Plot No. 137, Appertaining to Khata No. 538, situated in Village-Hisua Thana No. 69, P.S.- Hisua, District-Nawada.",
